& [Nodes] are source, manifest, selection review, explosion, canonical, justification, plan, signature, registry, matrix, slice, prerequisite stability, future implementation, tests, evidence, solution, proof, and future physical producer

& [Edges] define lineage
  + [source] selected_by [architecture_review]
  + [source] processed_to [explosion]
  + [explosion] refined_to [canonical]
  + [justification] supports [streaming_and_revalidation_selection]
  + [plan] orders [implementation_and_proof]
  + [stability] validates [binding_metadata]
  + [signature] authorizes [pure_implementation_only]
  + [implementation] will_satisfy [canonical_requirements]
  + [future_evidence] will_bind [clone_portable_artifacts]
  + [future_physical_producer] may_supply [chunks_and_stability_input] only under later authority

& [RetrievalTerms] include supplied content digest, SHA-256, streaming accumulator, consuming transition, exact length, content-read identity, entry-reference identity, stable binding, regular file, metadata length, output-only observation, and byte-origin nonclaim

& [NonEdges] are explicit
  + [absent] supplied chunk proves physical file origin
  + [absent] content-read identity proves one read or handle
  + [absent] stability binding proves content stability or physical order
  + [absent] digest proves authenticity, trust, signature, or immutability
  + [absent] canonical authority grants filesystem access, traversal, receipt, admission, or mutation

& [Dispatch] is exact
  + [applies_when] exact caller-supplied chunks require deterministic bounded SHA-256 derivation and structural association with revalidated supplied regular-file metadata
  + [does_not_apply] to byte acquisition, handles, paths, clocks, platform calls, physical order, provenance, traversal, Git projection, receipts, admission, mutation, sealing, cleanup, or promotion

